 {
  "simulant_id": "S018",
  "field": "lunar_sample_reference",
  "outcome": "withheld: refuted by verification",
  "problems": [
   "The extractor's 'stated by no opened document' is true only of the 8 group documents; the library does contain support. NEW6 Zou et al. 2024, p.1318: 'The European Astronaut Centre used basanite to produce a low-Ti mare simulant EAC-1A [21].' NEW7 Patzwald et al. 2025, p.203: '\u2026EAC-1 or EAC-1 A \u2026 is also used as a general-use low-Ti mare simulant [81].' Both are secondary statements citing Engelschi\u00f8n 2020, which itself says only 'mare'-type comparisons ('EAC-1A is most similar to the intermediate compositions of the Apollo 17 samples', p.4) and gives TiO2 2.4 wt% (p.4), which is low-Ti under Patzwald's definition (p.201: 'low-Ti (1.5\u20139 wt% TiO2)'). The extractor's point that Apollo 17 mare soils are high-Ti remains valid, so the curator must choose; but 'Low-Ti Mare' can be sourced to NEW6 (exact product name) with NEW7 as second support."
  ],
  "needs_review": false
 },
